# The trigger is independent of its source once on the stack (CR 113.7a, 608.2h): the Battler deals the damage as it last
# existed. Bot2 casts a Mox Ruby (first spell) and a Lightning Bolt at the Battler (second spell, so the trigger goes
# on the stack above it), then a second Lightning Bolt in response, which kills the Battler (3 damage on 3 toughness) before
# the trigger resolves. The trigger still deals 2 damage to Bot2 (18); the first Bolt has no target left and fizzles.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Hearthborn Battler
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Lightning Bolt
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Hearthborn Battler.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Hearthborn Battler)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Hearthborn Battler)
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Hearthborn Battler
Bot2.Life = 18
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt; Lightning Bolt
